{"term":"capital","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d912ad70bc43404b66","definition":"Money and wealth: the means to acquire or produce goods and services, especially in a non-barter system.","example":"Near-synonym: assets","pos":"noun","synonyms":["asset"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa6509c26b6acef393","definition":"Already-produced durable goods available for use as a factor of production, such as tools and bulldozers (equipment) and office buildings (structures).","example":"Near-synonym: assets","pos":"noun","synonyms":["asset"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06448a9791920bfcef","definition":"The capitalist class; investors considered collectively with respect to their societal (economic, political, cultural, etc.) influence.","example":"The markets crashing symbolized capital’s discontent with the tax reforms passed.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b221135e71e58a3ae3","definition":"A city designated as a legislative seat by the government or some other authority, often the city in which the government is located; otherwise the most important city within a country or a subdivision of it.","example":"Washington D.C. is the capital of the United States of America.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocati